// The difficulty levels of the computer opponent (WP9.4c): the shipped profiles that count as levels, in the
// order the start menu cycles them, and the one a player who never chose has. A level is the file name of a
// profile under `assets/ai/` without `.ron` (`easy` is `assets/ai/easy.ron`). This is the one place that
// lists them: `--ai <level>`, the start menu and the tests read it. The words the player reads
// ("Easy", "Normal", "Hard") are in `menu_look.ron`; the numbers of each level are in its profile file.
(
    // The match the start menu's "against the computer" entry plays (a name under `assets/matches`, as
    // `--match` takes it); its computer seats get the chosen level.
    ai_match: "m1_ai",
    default: "normal",
    levels: ["easy", "normal", "hard"],
)
